# Caddy: the domain in .env gets a free HTTPS certificate by itself (Let's Encrypt) and is forwarded to the app.
# Nothing else is needed: WebSockets (Streamlit needs them), the uploads and the "X-Forwarded-For" header that the
# app uses to count the free checks per person are all handled by Caddy.
#
# Keep the DNS record of this subdomain on "DNS only" (grey cloud) if the domain is on Cloudflare: with Cloudflare's
# proxy (orange cloud) every visitor looks like the same address to the app, and the "3 free checks a day" limit
# would count everybody as one person.

{$DOMAIN} {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy app:8501
}
